\p{\strong{3:08 PM}}
\hr
\question{What is the tradeoff of off-chip vs. on-chip memory?}
\answer{Look up Rent's rule.
  \ol{
    \li{On-chip bandwidth scales with die area (transistor count).}
    \li{Off-chip bandwidth scales with package pin count — which is limited by ball pitch and mechanical/thermal reality, and improves glacially.}
  }
}

